# Database Rules

- PostgreSQL is the system of record.
- Database schema must reflect the domain model; do not create tables only because they are convenient for one screen.
- Use consistent naming conventions documented in `docs/database/DATABASE.md`.
- Every schema change must be represented by an EF Core migration.
- Never edit an old migration to fix a new requirement if it may already have been applied; add a new migration.
- Define foreign keys and appropriate indexes for real query patterns.
- Avoid premature indexes and redundant columns.
- Preserve monetary values with appropriate decimal precision; never use floating point for money.
- Inventory quantities and stock movements must have an auditable source.
- Stock changes should be traceable to purchases, sales, transfers, or adjustments.
